source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: The rule takes its own line and the line below it is a block of its own inside the item, which a JFM item holding a rule has nowhere to put, so the block follows the list and jiro warns -- the reading a line control already gets there.
-- input.jira --
* ----
b
-- rendered.html --
<ul>
	<li><hr />
<p>b</p></li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
- ***

b
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "list",
    "Reason": "Jira keeps this line inside the list item above it; a JFM item holds nothing after its horizontal rule, so the line follows the list"
  }
]
